# Rust build output
/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
*.tmp
# Cargo.lock is committed: the exact dependency graph is part of the reproducible
# build, and reproducibility is the point of an integer-unit layout engine.

# cargo-fuzz build output. `fuzz/` is its own workspace and has its own .gitignore;
# these root-anchored entries keep `reuse lint` (which reads this file) in agreement
# with git about what is generated. Curated `fuzz/corpus/` seeds are committed.
/fuzz/target/
/fuzz/artifacts/
/fuzz/coverage/

# cargo-mutants working output.
/mutants.out/
/mutants.out.old/
/mutants-*

# The six matrices of Appendices B through E are published only as PDF, and a PDF is
# not a source this project derives anything from (docs/adr/0009). A developer
# transcribing one fetches the file here; spec/PROVENANCE.toml records its digest, so
# `attest --digests` can prove the bytes are the ones this repository was written
# against without the PDF ever entering the history.
/spec/upstream/

# dune build output for engines/. The dune project root is the repository root
# (a dune rule cannot depend on a file above it, and the engines read spec/), so
# the build directory lands here rather than under engines/. The engine binary
# the conformance runner is given lives inside it:
# _build/default/engines/ocaml/bin/jlreq_ocaml_engine.exe
/_build/
/engines/ocaml/_opam/

# mise local overrides (per-developer, never committed)
/mise.local.toml
/.mise.local.toml

# Editor / OS
/.idea/
/.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.claude/
